## Why This Is Asked

This question tests depth in CAPA design for cross-tenant data exposure caused by policy migration bugs in a real-time data mesh. It evaluates the ability to model evidence, define a region-aware lifecycle, implement a minimal API, and build measurable containment strategies plus RCA artifacts and canary rollouts.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model capturing evidence, tenant IDs, policy metadata, dashboards, and timestamps
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine for CAPA progression
- RBAC/policy migration risks in real-time data platforms
- Minimal REST API design to link logs/traces to CAPA records
- Canary rollout and region-validated testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal CAPA creation endpoint
app.post('/api/capa', async (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, tenants, dashboards, policyHash, evidence } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA, link logs/traces, trigger workflow
  res.status(201).send({ id: incidentId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate cross-tenant exposure detection at scale across regions?
- What data retention and privacy considerations would you encode in the CAPA API?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around operational risk in alert routing, including change control, cross-tenant impact, and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model (evidence, lineage, owners)
- Lifecycle with detect/contain/remediate/verify and SLAs
- Canary-based rollback and change control
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, MTTR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express-like minimal CAPA create endpoint (illustrative)
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const capa = req.body;
  // persist CAPA with evidence, lineage, owners
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', ...capa });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollback plan for alert-rule changes?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate containment and prevent recurrence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around data governance, cross-region containment, and traceability after a data-leak fault in a deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and evidence tagging
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle gates
- REST API design for CAPA management with linked logs/traces
- Regional leakage metrics and false positive handling
- RCA templates and canary rollback for data sinks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model in TypeScript
type CAPA = {
  capa_id: string;
  incident_time: string;
  data_class: string;
  evidence_refs: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owner: string;
  remediation: string;
  status: 'IDENTIFY'|'CONTAIN'|'INVESTIGATE'|'REMEDIATE'|'VERIFY'|'CLOSED';
  RCA_id?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with an existing audit log system?
- How would you enforce access controls for CAPA modification?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to handle CAPA at multi-tenant scale with data provenance, cost control, and isolation. Requires concrete data model, lifecycle, API surface, and measurable metrics.

## Key Concepts
- Data provenance and lineage
- Tenant isolation vs shared infra
- Cost-aware remediation
- Lifecycle state machine
- REST API design and observability

